# Two code owners, so neither one's own pull request can pass on the automated
# review's approval alone: GitHub waives the code-owner rule when the author is
# the only owner, and the review's approval would then count.
# Review is required on everything, and specifically on the paths where a
# mistake is not visible in a plan: the workflows that decide which identity
# CI may request, the _setup roots that define what those identities can do,
# and the rules the automated review applies. A change there is a change to
# who can change production, or to what a review lets through.
#
# Code-owner approval is required by the dev ruleset, so an approval from the
# automated review never counts toward a merge: only these people's does.

*                               @drn1996 @frubble-platform
/.github/workflows/**           @drn1996 @frubble-platform
/.github/claude-review/**       @drn1996 @frubble-platform
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @drn1996 @frubble-platform
/terraform/live/**/_setup/      @drn1996 @frubble-platform
